E
book~
When you open his black, leather-bound book, you realize why it is so very
thin.  It contains only a single, hand-written page.  The writing reads as
follows:

        "By the time anyone finds this writing, I, Kralus, shall be deeply
entrenched in the Sleep of Ages.  Do not disturb me, or as punishment I shall
destroy you as I destroyed those who I loved so dearly, so long ago.  Spare me
the agony of waking and remembering the justice which had to be done.  They
were my people, who worshipped and loved me. They asked for my blessing upon
everything they did and I gave it to them gladly for I cherished them greatly.
When they went to war, they prayed for my protection from harm and for my
direction in battle, so they might treat their opponents fairly and with
dignity.  For many hundreds of years and then many hundreds more, they were my
children and I tended them as such.  As those years rolled by, I began to
distance myself from them.  I tried to convince myself it was to allow them to
make their own decisions so they might grow in wisdom but I knew that for the
lie it was.  My heart grew increasingly weary as I watched each generation age
and die, as I watched those precious flames of mortal splendor I had come to
know and love slowly dim and then flicker into nothingness.  For a great many
years, they held true to my teachings and conducted themselves as if I was
there with them.  This brought me great joy but also no small amount of
sorrow.  My children had grown and they no longer had a need for me.  With
this in mind, I began to find other diversions and would sometimes spend
several years away before I would visit.  It was during one of these long
periods things became grave.  My children learned a hard lesson about
treachery by becoming trusting victims.  What happened was not really all that
important but the lessoned learned was.  Having witnessed deceit first-hand,
they began to put it in to practice.  At first it was in small ways, but as
evil is prone to do, it grew exponentially.  When I returned to them, they had
become a vicious army of greedy demons who fought simply for profit.  They no
longer treated their enemies with dignity and respect, instead raping and
pillaging for whatever loot they could scavenge.  I went immediately to the
high priest in this very temple and ordered an immediate end to their savage
cruelty. But this priest was as much of a villian as the worst and openly
defied me.  My anger at his insolence was so immense I killed him with a word
there on the spot but that didn't begin to satisfy the anger he had stirred
deep inside my soul.  I reached out to each and all of my childrens' children
and layed a geas upon them to return to the temple to face my wrath, though
not all survived their travels, such was the urgency of my summons.  Never had
the walls of the worship hall had to magically expand to accomodate the number
of people it held that day.  When I saw them all assembled, I was suddenly
reminded of their ancestors and the heat of my anger was quickly snuffed.  So,
I began to talk to them, to try to teach them the folly of their behavior but
they cared little for what I had to say.  Again my anger burned and I began to
rail at them, scolding them for and forbidding their evil doings.  They
scorned me, said they didn't hold to the beliefs of their forefathers nor
their love for me.  They demanded I leave them alone as I had done before. At
that last insult, the heat of my anger burst forth in a rush incinerating an
entire race in an instant.  The once beautiful walls of the hall where their
ancestors had gathered to worship were suddenly stained a deep, light-stealing
black from the horribleness of their sins.

        That is the story of my people.  I now sleep to forget although not
a millenium will take away the memories of my beautiful ones.  So if you value
your existence or possess any kind of decency whatsoever, please, leave me to
my misery.                                                      



                                          Kralus
~
B
